        "statement": "Worked computation of the transition between two inertial charts. Let (A,V,eta,C^+) be an oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski space with inertial frames (o;e_a) and (o';e'_a) and charts x, x', and write e'_a = sum_b M^b_a e_b with M invertible. Then for every event p, x'(p) = M^{-1}(x(p) - x(o')) = M^{-1} x(p) + b with b := -M^{-1} x(o'), so the transition is affine. Explicit 1+1-dimensional case: V = R^2 with eta(v,w) = -v^0 w^0 + v^1 w^1, o = o' = 0, e_0 = (1,0), e_1 = (0,1), and the boosted inertial frame e'_0 = (cosh r, sinh r), e'_1 = (sinh r, cosh r) for real r, which satisfies eta(e'_0,e'_0) = -1, eta(e'_1,e'_1) = +1, eta(e'_0,e'_1) = 0 and det M = cosh^2 r - sinh^2 r = 1 with M the matrix with columns e'_0, e'_1 in the e-basis. The transition matrix is M^{-1} = [[cosh r, -sinh r],[-sinh r, cosh r]], and x'(o) = 0, x'(x^{-1}(1,0)) = (cosh r, -sinh r).",
